            },
            "text": "In India the ultimate temple, since times ancient, has always been the human body."
          },
          {
            "bullet": false,
            "level": 0,
            "runs": [
              {
                "style": {
                  "alignment": "l",
                  "bold": null,
                  "color": "#FFFFFF",
                  "font_family": "Trebuchet MS",
                  "italic": null,
                  "language": "en-IN",
                  "size_pt": 20.0,
                  "underline": null
                },
                "text": "The Hindu temple is perceived as a link between man and God, between the earthly life and the divine life, between the actual and the ideal."
              }
            ],
            "style": {
              "alignment": "l",
              "bold": null,
              "color": "#FFFFFF",
              "font_family": "Trebuchet MS",
              "italic": null,
              "language": null,
              "size_pt": 18.0,
              "underline": null
            },
            "text": "The Hindu temple is perceived as a link between man and God, between the earthly life and the divine life, between the actual and the ideal."
          },
          {
            "bullet": false,
            "level": 0,
            "runs": [
              {
                "style": {
                  "alignment": "l",
                  "bold": null,
                  "color": "#FFFFFF",
                  "font_family": "Trebuchet MS",
                  "italic": null,
                  "language": "en-IN",
                  "size_pt": 20.0,
                  "underline": null
                },
                "text": "The origin of all the classical dances of India has been the Hindu temple; it is in the temple that they were conceived and nourished and it is in the temple itself that they acquired their full stature. Fostered by religion, they continue to be an intrinsic part of worship in the temples even today."
              }
            ],
            "style": {
              "alignment": "l",
              "bold": null,
              "color": "#FFFFFF",
              "font_family": "Trebuchet MS",
              "italic": null,
              "language": null,
              "size_pt": 18.0,
              "underline": null
            },
            "text": "The origin of all the classical dances of India has been the Hindu temple; it is in the temple that they were conceived and nourished and it is in the temple itself that they acquired their full stature. Fostered by religion, they continue to be an intrinsic part of worship in the temples even today."
          },
          {
            "bullet": false,
            "level": 0,
            "runs": [
              {
                "style": {
                  "alignment": "l",
                  "bold": null,
                  "color": "#FFFFFF",
                  "font_family": "Trebuchet MS",
                  "italic": null,
                  "language": "en-IN",
                  "size_pt": 20.0,
                  "underline": null
                },
                "text": "The intangible, born and nurtured in the tangible that is built on the metaphysical plan of the cosmic intangible, contains within it, the entire structure of the tangible itself. Neither without the other."
              }
            ],
            "style": {
              "alignment": "l",
              "bold": null,
              "color": "#FFFFFF",
              "font_family": "Trebuchet MS",
              "italic": null,
              "language": null,
              "size_pt": 18.0,
              "underline": null
            },
            "text": "The intangible, born and nurtured in the tangible that is built on the metaphysical plan of the cosmic intangible, contains within it, the entire structure of the tangible itself. Neither without the other."
          },
          {
            "bullet": false,
            "level": 0,
            "runs": [
              {
                "style": {
                  "alignment": "l",
